WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.004 --> 00:00:14.088
"It's a nice day for a hike," said Dad.

2
00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:18.702
"Yeah," said Oliver.

3
00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:23.701
"I want to hike to the top of a mountain!"

4
00:00:23.702 --> 00:00:30.692
"Hiking up a mountain is hard," said Mom.

5
00:00:30.693 --> 00:00:38.787
"I can do it!" said Oliver.

6
00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:44.316
Dad drove the car to the mountain.

7
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:51.139
Everybody put on backpacks.

8
00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.093
"I can carry the bottles of water," said Harry.

9
00:00:55.094 --> 00:00:59.431
"I can carry the apples," said Emmy.

10
00:00:59.432 --> 00:01:03.885
"I can carry the first aid kit," said Mom.

11
00:01:03.886 --> 00:01:07.649
"I can carry the map," said Oliver.

12
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.555
Dad laughed.

13
00:01:11.556 --> 00:01:15.211
"I have nothing to carry!" he said.

14
00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:18.585
Everybody hiked on the trail.

15
00:01:18.586 --> 00:01:24.694
The trail went up.

16
00:01:24.695 --> 00:01:29.025
"Are you tired?" Mom asked Oliver.

17
00:01:29.026 --> 00:01:31.880
"Nope," said Oliver.

18
00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:35.441
"This is easy!"

19
00:01:35.442 --> 00:01:39.191
The family hiked some more.

20
00:01:39.192 --> 00:01:45.271
Oliver huffed and puffed.

21
00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:49.452
"Are you tired?" asked Emmy.

22
00:01:49.453 --> 00:01:54.406
"Just a little bit," said Oliver.

23
00:01:54.407 --> 00:01:58.472
The trail got very steep.

24
00:01:58.473 --> 00:02:02.399
Oliver started to walk slowly.

25
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.609
"Are you tired?" asked Harry.

26
00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:10.782
"I can make it," said Oliver.

27
00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:17.980
At last the trail stopped.

28
00:02:17.981 --> 00:02:23.099
"We are at the top," said Dad.

29
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:32.319
"I made it!" said Oliver.

30
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.057
"Now we hike down the mountain," said Mom.

31
00:02:37.058 --> 00:02:39.916
Oliver sat down.

32
00:02:39.917 --> 00:02:45.359
"I'm too tired," said Oliver.

33
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:51.155
"Now I have something to carry," said Dad.

34
00:02:51.156 --> 00:02:58.291
"I can carry Oliver!"

